INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(1,'47e3f24e',1,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/','The @cloudflare/computer package provides an agent runtime where the details and mechanics of what code runs in an isolate, a container sandbox, or a web browser are handled by the platform, allowing for a simpler abstraction and more efficient compute primitives. It offers a durable filesystem, tools for file manipulation, and execution runtimes, including isolate-based and container-based environments.','The goal of understanding what @cloudflare/computer provides is partially met, but the goal of understanding how Workflows durable execution works is not yet addressed.',1786405382639,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(2,'9445e0f0',1,'https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-computer/','Cloudflare Computer provides a platform for running code at the edge, with @cloudflare/computer being a JavaScript runtime environment, but details on durable execution are not found in the provided source','Goal 1 is partially met as we have an understanding of @cloudflare/computer, but Goal 2 remains unmet',1786405493190,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(3,'9445e0f0',2,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/','According to the Cloudflare Workflows documentation, Workflows provide a way to define a series of tasks that can be executed in a specific order, but details on durable execution are still not found in the provided source. The ''Rules of Workflows'' page explains how to structure Workflows, but does not explicitly mention durable execution.','The goal of understanding what @cloudflare/computer provides is partially met, but the goal of understanding how Workflows durable execution works remains unmet.',1786405499303,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(4,'faacbc1d',1,'https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-computer/','The @cloudflare/computer package provides an agent runtime that handles the details of code execution in an isolate, container sandbox, or web browser, allowing agents to work with a filesystem, shell, tools, and packages, and optimizing for efficiency and scalability. It introduces a simpler abstraction for combining isolates and containers, and provides a durable filesystem and execution runtime that can be used with git repositories, storage buckets, or any files, with tools for reading, writing, and editing files, and fine-grained control over changes made by the agent.','The goal of understanding what @cloudflare/computer provides is partially met, but the goal of understanding how Workflows durable execution works is not yet addressed.',1786405612685,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(5,'faacbc1d',2,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/','Workflows durable execution works by allowing each step to be self-contained and individually retryable, with the ability to emit state that allows a Workflow to persist and continue from that step even if it fails due to a network or infrastructure issue. Steps should be designed to be idempotent, meaning that they can be applied multiple times without changing the result beyond the initial application, and should not rely on state outside of a step as Workflows may hibernate and lose all in-memory state.','The goal of understanding how Workflows durable execution works is now met, but the goal of understanding what @cloudflare/computer provides is already met from prior findings.',1786405667497,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(6,'ff663b9d',1,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/','In Cloudflare Workflows, steps are self-contained and individually retryable, with the ability to emit state that allows a Workflow to persist and continue from that step even if it fails due to network or infrastructure issues. To ensure durability, steps should be idempotent, meaning they can be applied multiple times without changing the result beyond the initial application. This can be achieved by checking if an operation is still needed before performing it, as seen in the example of checking if a customer was already charged before attempting to charge them again.','The goal of understanding how steps and retries work in Workflows is partially met, but the goal of understanding how sleep works is not yet met.',1786405821152,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(7,'ff663b9d',2,'https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-computer/','The @cloudflare/computer package provides a durable filesystem and execution runtime, allowing agents to operate on files with various execution environments, including isolates and containers. This package seems to address the need for durable execution in Cloudflare Workflows, but the provided excerpts do not explicitly mention how steps, retries, and sleep work in conjunction with this package.','The goal of understanding how steps, retries, and sleep work in Workflows is still not fully met, as the new excerpts focus on the @cloudflare/computer package and its features, rather than directly addressing the Workflows'' mechanics.',1786405889412,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(8,'ee08ca83',1,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/reference/metadata-filtering/','Vectorize namespaces and metadata filtering are two methods to narrow the vector search space for a query. A namespace filter is applied before metadata filter(s), and a vector can only be part of a single namespace. Metadata filtering allows for more flexibility, supporting multiple key-value pairs and different data types. To use metadata filtering, a metadata index must be created, which can be done for properties of type string, integer, or float64.','The goal of understanding Vectorize namespaces and metadata filtering is partially met, but more information is needed to fully understand the capabilities and limitations of metadata filtering.',1786405980660,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(9,'ee08ca83',2,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/best-practices/insert-vectors/','Vectorize supports metadata filtering with multiple key-value pairs and different data types, including string, integer, and float64, and metadata indexes can be created for properties of these types, with a limit of 10KiB of metadata per vector and 10 metadata indexes per Vectorize index, as seen in excerpts [new 2] and [mem 2]. Additionally, namespace filtering is applied before metadata filtering, and a vector can only be part of a single namespace, as stated in excerpts [new 4] and [mem 1].','The goal of understanding Vectorize namespaces and metadata filtering is partially met, with more details on metadata indexing and filtering, but further clarification on namespace management and optimization is still needed.',1786406049552,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(10,'bf803830',1,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/platform/pricing/','The free tier of Vectorize has a limit of 30 million queried vector dimensions per month and 5 million stored vector dimensions, with additional usage billed at $0.01 per million queried vector dimensions and $0.05 per 100 million stored vector dimensions','The goal of understanding free tier vector dimension limits is partially met, but the exact dimensions limit per vector is not specified in the provided excerpts',1786406103150,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(11,'bf803830',2,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/llms.txt','The free tier vector dimension limits for Vectorize are 30 million queried vector dimensions per month and 5 million stored vector dimensions, as stated in the recalled excerpts from earlier sources, but the newly read source does not provide new information on this topic, instead pointing to the ''Limits'' page for account, index, and vector limits for Vectorize on Free and Paid plans.','The goal of understanding free tier vector dimension limits is partially met, but the new source does not provide additional information to fully satisfy the goal.',1786406170242,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(12,'bf803830',3,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/platform/limits/index.md','The maximum dimensions per vector for Vectorize is 1536 dimensions, with 32 bits precision, as stated in the Limits page for account, index, and vector limits for Vectorize on Free and Paid plans.','The goal of understanding free tier vector dimension limits is partially met, but the specific limit for the free tier is not found in the newly read source.',1786406237062,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(13,'bf803830',4,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/platform/pricing/index.md','The free tier of Vectorize has a limit of 30 million queried vector dimensions per month and 5 million stored vector dimensions. The maximum dimensions per vector for Vectorize is 1536 dimensions, with 32 bits precision.','The goal of understanding free tier vector dimension limits is now met.',1786406303923,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(14,'caa9dd72',1,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/platform/pricing/','The free tier of Vectorize has a limit of 30 million queried vector dimensions per month and 5 million stored vector dimensions, with additional usage billed at $0.01 per million queried vector dimensions and $0.05 per 100 million stored vector dimensions','The goal of understanding free tier vector dimension limits is partially met, but the exact dimensions limit per vector is not specified',1786406337426,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(15,'b73f81e5',1,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/platform/pricing/index.md','Vectorize pricing is based on queried and stored vector dimensions, with costs calculated as ((queried vectors + stored vectors) * dimensions * ($0.01 / 1,000,000)) + (stored vectors * dimensions * ($0.05 / 100,000,000)), and the service does not charge for CPU, memory, or data transfer/egress','The goal of confirming neuron accounting is not met as the provided excerpts do not mention neuron accounting, but rather vector dimensions',1786407389821,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(16,'823db4a8',1,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/platform/pricing/index.md','The source indicates that Vectorize bills are based on the total number of vector dimensions queried and stored, with specific pricing metrics outlined in the billing metrics table. For example, the Workers Free plan includes 30 million queried vector dimensions and 5 million stored vector dimensions per month, while the Workers Paid plan includes 50 million queried vector dimensions and 10 million stored vector dimensions per month, with additional usage billed at $0.01 per million queried vector dimensions and $0.05 per 100 million stored vector dimensions.','The goal of confirming spend is recorded is partially met, as the source provides information on how Vectorize billing works, but does not explicitly address neuron accounting.',1786407436343,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(17,'a06d8b5a',1,'https://developers.cloudflare.com/vectorize/llms.txt','The provided excerpts do not mention a ''budget guard'' or any mechanism for halting a loop based on budget constraints. The excerpts focus on Cloudflare''s Vectorize product, its features, and usage.','The goal of confirming loop halts on budget is not met as the excerpts do not provide relevant information.',1786407472973,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(18,'19ac529b',1,'https://smallbizai.au/australian-ai-companies-complete-guide-by-industry-2026/','Australian AI startups concentrate in various sectors, including fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with companies like Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker being notable examples. The ecosystem splits between AI-native companies, such as Baraja and Carbar, and AI-enabled incumbents, like WiseTech and REA Group. Sydney is a major hub for these companies, with many being headquartered there.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with some sectors and company types identified, but more work is needed to fully understand the ecosystem and its funding landscape.',1786408545819,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(19,'19ac529b',2,'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_and_technology_in_Australia','The newly read source does not provide specific information about the Australian AI startup ecosystem, its sectors, funding, or geographic clusters. However, recalled sources suggest that Australian AI startups are active in various sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with notable examples including Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker. The ecosystem is distinguished between AI-native companies like Baraja and Carbar, and AI-enabled incumbents like WiseTech and REA Group.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met through recalled sources, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved due to lack of relevant information in the newly read source.',1786408682863,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(20,'19ac529b',3,'https://www.csiro.au/en/research/technology-space/ai','The newly read source from CSIRO does not provide specific information about the Australian AI startup ecosystem, but recalled sources suggest that Australian AI startups are active in various sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with notable examples including Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker. The ecosystem splits between AI-native companies like Baraja and Carbar, and AI-enabled incumbents like WiseTech and REA Group.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved as the newly read source does not provide information on funding, geographic clusters, or specific examples of companies in each sector.',1786408812318,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(21,'19ac529b',4,'https://www.startmate.com/portfolio','The Startmate portfolio provides examples of Australian AI startups across various sectors, including proptech (e.g., Landid), healthcare (e.g., Medlo, Doccy), and education (e.g., Learna), but does not offer specific insights into the funding landscape, geographic clusters, or growth rates of these sectors. Recalled sources suggest that Sydney is a major hub for these companies, with many being headquartered there, and that the ecosystem splits between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with some sectors and company examples identified, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved, as the funding landscape, geographic clusters, and growth rates are not clearly addressed in the provided excerpts.',1786408940781,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(22,'19ac529b',5,'https://www.cutthroughventure.com/reports','Australian AI startups are concentrated in sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with companies like Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker being notable examples. The ecosystem splits between AI-native companies, such as Baraja and Carbar, and AI-enabled incumbents, like WiseTech and REA Group. Sydney is a major hub for these companies, with many being headquartered there. Additionally, the funding landscape for Australian AI startups is characterized by a mix of venture capital investments and crowdfunding, with some notable recent funding rounds including Aerotruth''s $1.3 million Seed funding and MagicBrief''s $2m funding for creative marketing tools.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with some information available on the sectors and distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved, requiring further research on the funding landscape, geographic clusters, and specific examples of companies in each sector.',1786409071474,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(23,'19ac529b',6,'https://www.startupdaily.net/','Newly funded Australian AI startups include Vexev, which raised $8.6m for vascular ultrasound and AI, Enrola, which raised $2.1m for AI sales-tech, and Firmus, which raised $2.85 billion at a $15B valuation for its AI data centre plan. These funding rounds suggest a growing interest in AI applications in healthcare and data infrastructure.','Goals 1 and 3 are partially met, as the newly read source provides information on specific sectors and funding rounds, but more information is needed to fully understand the ecosystem and its geographic clusters.',1786409208310,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(24,'19ac529b',7,'https://www.innovationaus.com/','The Australian AI startup ecosystem is characterized by a mix of AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, with notable examples including Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker, and a funding landscape that includes venture capital investments and crowdfunding, as seen in recent funding rounds such as Aerotruth''s $1.3 million Seed funding and MagicBrief''s $2m funding','Goals 1, 2, and 3 are partially met, with information on the main sectors, distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, and funding landscape, but goals 4 and 5 remain unresolved, with limited information on geographic clusters and growth rates',1786409341440,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(25,'19ac529b',8,'https://blackbird.vc/portfolio','Blackbird.vc has invested in over 130 ambitious companies, including some in stealth, and is focused on supporting founders tackling the world''s greatest problems, with a portfolio that includes companies in sectors such as healthcare, space, and farming, leveraging artificial intelligence to create a more sustainable future, as seen in their investment in Superstat and Tracksuit, which acquired Hall to add AI visibility to its brand tracking platform','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with identified sectors including fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, and a distinction between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, but goals 3, 4, and 5 are still unresolved',1786409469928,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(26,'19ac529b',9,'https://techcouncil.com.au/','The Tech Council of Australia highlights the importance of promoting skilled migration, training pathways, and future-ready education policies to build a strong and diverse tech workforce, which is crucial for the growth of the Australian AI startup ecosystem. Additionally, the council supports balanced, future-focused regulation that fosters innovation while ensuring security, privacy, and responsible AI development.','Goals 2 and 3 are partially met, as the ecosystem splits between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, and the funding landscape includes venture capital investments and crowdfunding, but more information is needed to fully understand the main sectors, growth rates, and geographic clusters.',1786409597343,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(27,'19ac529b',10,'https://www.smartcompany.com.au/','The newly read source provides information on various Australian businesses, including those in the retail and technology sectors, but does not offer specific insights into the Australian AI startup ecosystem. However, it mentions SafetyCulture, which has unveiled new AI features, and PsiQuantum, which has landed a $179.2 million DARPA quantum computing deal. Recalled sources suggest that Australian AI startups are active in various sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with notable examples including Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, as the ecosystem''s sectors and the distinction between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents are identified, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved.',1786409727120,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(28,'19ac529b',11,'https://www.austrade.gov.au/','The newly read source from Austrade does not provide specific information about the Australian AI startup ecosystem, but recalled sources suggest that Australian AI startups are active in various sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with notable examples including Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker. The ecosystem splits between AI-native companies like Baraja and Carbar, and AI-enabled incumbents like WiseTech and REA Group.','Goals 1, 2, and 3 are partially met, but goals 4 and 5 remain unresolved as the newly read source does not provide information on geographic clusters or distinguish between AI-native and AI-enabled companies in the context of the Australian AI startup ecosystem.',1786409855318,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(34,'0d5ed883',1,'https://smallbizai.au/australian-ai-companies-complete-guide-by-industry-2026/','The Australian AI startup ecosystem consists of companies in various sectors, including fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education. Companies like Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker are notable examples. The ecosystem can be split into AI-native companies, founded in 2016 or later, and AI-enabled incumbents, founded before 2016. AirTree Ventures is one of the most respected venture capital firms in Australia, increasingly focused on AI.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with some sectors and company types identified, but more work is needed to fully understand the ecosystem and its funding landscape.',1786410912841,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(35,'0d5ed883',2,'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_and_technology_in_Australia','The newly read source does not provide specific information about the Australian AI startup ecosystem, its sectors, funding, or geographic clusters. However, prior findings and recalled sources suggest that the ecosystem includes companies like Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker, and can be split into AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, with AirTree Ventures being a key venture capital firm. Notable sectors include fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with companies like Athena, Brighte, and Airtasker operating in these areas.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met through prior findings, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved due to lack of relevant information in the newly read source.',1786411045035,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(36,'0d5ed883',3,'https://www.csiro.au/en/research/technology-space/ai','The newly read source from CSIRO does not provide specific information about the Australian AI startup ecosystem, but prior findings and recalled sources suggest that the ecosystem includes companies in various sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with notable examples including Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker. The ecosystem can be split into AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, with AirTree Ventures being a key venture capital firm.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with some information available on sectors and the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved.',1786411177162,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(37,'0d5ed883',4,'https://www.startmate.com/portfolio','Startmate''s portfolio includes various Australian AI startups across sectors like fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with examples such as Puralink, Matilda, and Landid, which can be classified as either AI-native or AI-enabled companies, but the source does not provide specific information on funding, geographic clusters, or distinctions between these company types','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved, with some sectors and companies identified, but funding, geographic clusters, and distinctions between AI-native and AI-enabled companies still unclear',1786411305966,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(38,'0d5ed883',5,'https://www.cutthroughventure.com/reports','Australian AI startups are raising significant funding, with $810m raised in Q2 and a $4b year, driven by the AI boom, and companies like Athena, Brighte, and Airtasker are operating in notable sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with AirTree Ventures being a key venture capital firm, as seen in sources like https://www.innovationaus.com/ and https://smallbizai.au/australian-ai-companies-complete-guide-by-industry-2026/','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with identified sectors and a distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved, requiring further information on funding, geographic clusters, and specific company examples',1786411440040,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(39,'0d5ed883',6,'https://www.startupdaily.net/','The Australian AI startup ecosystem includes companies like Vexev, Enrola, and Firmus, which are operating in sectors such as medical robotics, sales-tech, and AI data centres. These companies are raising significant funding, with examples like Vexev''s $8.6m raise and Firmus''s $2.85 billion raise at a $15B valuation. The ecosystem can be split into AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, with AirTree Ventures being a key venture capital firm. Notable sectors include fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with companies like Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker operating in these areas.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with the identification of main sectors and the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, but goals 3, 4, and 5 are still unresolved, requiring further information on funding, geographic clusters, and example companies for each major sector.',1786411569701,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(40,'0d5ed883',7,'https://www.innovationaus.com/','South Australia is actively pursuing AI investments, as evidenced by its new partnership with OpenAI, which could lead to fresh research collaborations, data centre investment, and a skills makeover for the state''s public sector. This suggests that South Australia is a notable geographic cluster for AI activity in Australia.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with notable sectors and company distinctions identified, but goals 3, 4, and 5 remain unresolved, as the newly read source does not provide specific information on funding, geographic clusters, or example companies beyond prior findings.',1786411699233,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(41,'0d5ed883',8,'https://blackbird.vc/portfolio','Blackbird.vc has invested in over 130 ambitious companies, including those in the Australian AI startup ecosystem, with a focus on backing founders doing their life''s work and tackling the world''s greatest problems, across sectors such as healthcare, space, and farming, but specific details on the sectors, funding, or geographic clusters are not provided','Goals 1, 2, and 4 remain unresolved, while goal 3 has some progress with the identification of Blackbird.vc as an active investor, but more information is needed to fully understand the funding landscape',1786411828300,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(42,'0d5ed883',9,'https://techcouncil.com.au/','The Tech Council of Australia highlights the importance of a thriving tech-enabled economy, with 949,000 Australians employed in tech-related jobs and the industry contributing $248 billion to GDP. The council also mentions the need to support balanced, future-focused regulation that fosters innovation while ensuring security, privacy, and responsible AI development. Notable alliances include the Australian Quantum Alliance (AQA), Consumer Energy Tech Alliance (CETA), and National Security Tech Alliance (NSTA), which may indicate emerging sectors or areas of focus within the Australian AI startup ecosystem.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with the identification of various sectors and the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, but more information is needed to fully understand the ecosystem''s composition and geographic clusters.',1786411961481,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(43,'0d5ed883',10,'https://www.smartcompany.com.au/','The newly read source does not provide specific information about the Australian AI startup ecosystem, but mentions companies like SafetyCulture, which has unveiled new AI features, and Canva, which has become the world''s second most-visited AI platform. This suggests that AI is being adopted in various sectors, but more information is needed to determine the main sectors, funding landscape, and geographic clusters.','Goals 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 are still unresolved, as the newly read source does not provide sufficient information to identify the main sectors, distinguish between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, map the funding landscape, identify geographic clusters, or surface named example companies for each major sector.',1786412091913,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(44,'0d5ed883',11,'https://www.ausbiz.com.au/','The Australian AI startup ecosystem can be split into AI-native companies, founded in 2016 or later, and AI-enabled incumbents, founded before 2016, with notable sectors including fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, and companies like Canva, Atlassian, and Airtasker operating in these areas, as seen in sources like https://smallbizai.au/australian-ai-companies-complete-guide-by-industry-2026/ and https://www.startmate.com/portfolio','Goals 1 and 2 are partially met, with notable sectors and company types identified, but more information is needed to determine the fastest-growing sectors and fully distinguish between AI-native and AI-enabled companies',1786412219048,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(45,'0d5ed883',12,'https://www.airtree.vc/','AirTree Ventures is a key venture capital firm in the Australian AI startup ecosystem, backing Aussie and Kiwi founders building iconic technology companies, with a focus on AI-native companies founded in 2016 or later, as seen in https://www.airtree.vc/ and https://smallbizai.au/australian-ai-companies-complete-guide-by-industry-2026/','Goals 2 and 3 are partially met, with the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies clarified, and AirTree Ventures identified as a key investor, but more information is needed on the main sectors, funding landscape, and geographic clusters',1786412351845,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(46,'2ff3e9c4',1,'https://www.startupdaily.net/','The Australian AI startup ecosystem includes companies such as Millibeam, which received $4.6 million in government grants for its drone jammer, and SafetyCulture, which is rebranding as Mitti with a focus on AI. Other companies mentioned include Enrola, which raised $2.1 million for its AI sales agents, and Firmus, which raised $2.85 billion at a $15 billion valuation. The South Australian premier has also signed a deal with OpenAI.','The research has made progress on identifying sectors and named companies in the Australian AI startup ecosystem, but the funding landscape is not yet fully mapped.',1786412787712,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(47,'2ff3e9c4',2,'https://www.startmate.com/portfolio','The Australian AI startup ecosystem encompasses various sectors, including healthcare, education, and real estate, with companies such as Landid, which harnesses AI to digitise property details, and Medlo, which connects doctors with short- and long-term roles. Other notable companies include Vulnetix, which builds an intelligent monitoring layer for cybersecurity, and Duohub, which helps non-technical people build AI agents. These companies are part of Startmate''s portfolio, which has invested in over 300 startups with a collective value of over $4.5 billion.','The goal of identifying sectors and named companies is partially met, while the goal of mapping the funding landscape is still unresolved as the provided excerpts do not offer detailed funding information for each company.',1786412794223,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(48,'2ff3e9c4',3,'https://blackbird.vc/portfolio','Blackbird has invested in over 130 ambitious companies, including those in the AI sector, such as Superstat, Tracksuit, and Halter, which leverage AI for sports data, brand tracking, and sustainable farming respectively. This suggests a diverse funding landscape with investments in various AI applications.','The goal of identifying sectors and named companies is partially met, with new companies and sectors emerging, while the funding landscape goal is also partially met with insights into Blackbird''s investments, but more information is needed to fully understand the landscape.',1786412800994,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(49,'76fb1813',1,'https://smallbizai.au/australian-ai-companies-complete-guide-by-industry-2026/','Australian AI startups concentrate in various sectors, including fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with companies like Athena, Archistar, and Cluey Learning being examples. The funding landscape includes investors like AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia, with companies like Canva and Atlassian being notable examples of AI-native and AI-enabled companies, respectively.','Goals 1, 2, 3, and 5 have been partially answered, while goals 4 remains open',1786417632047,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(50,'76fb1813',2,'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_and_technology_in_Australia','Not stated in the sources read so far regarding the specific growth rates of sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate, the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies in the ecosystem, the most active investors and typical funding stages, or the differentiation of geographic clusters in Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, and Perth.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with sectors identified, but growth rates and other goals remain open.',1786417704075,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(51,'76fb1813',3,'https://www.csiro.au/en/research/technology-space/ai','The CSIRO website provides educational content on AI, including a video that explains how AI works, but does not provide specific information on the Australian AI startup ecosystem, its sectors, funding, or geographic clusters. However, recalled sources mention companies like Athena, Archistar, and Cluey Learning as examples of AI startups in various sectors, including fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education.','Goals 1, 3, 4, and 5 are still open, while goal 2 has some information from recalled sources, but the new source does not provide additional information on the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies.',1786417773929,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(52,'76fb1813',4,'https://www.startmate.com/portfolio','Startmate has invested in over 300 startups with a collective portfolio value of over $4.5 billion, including companies like Puralink, Matilda, and Landid, which operate in various sectors such as robotics, migration, and proptech. This suggests a diverse range of AI startups in Australia, but does not provide specific information on growth rates, funding stages, or geographic clusters.','Goals 1 and 3 are partially answered, with some information on sectors and funding, but goals 2, 4, and 5 remain open. The distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, geographic clusters, and example companies for each major sector are still unclear.',1786417841884,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(53,'76fb1813',5,'https://www.cutthroughventure.com/reports','Australian AI startups concentrate in sectors like fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with examples including Athena, Archistar, and Cluey Learning. The funding landscape includes investors like AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia, with companies like Canva and Atlassian being notable examples of AI-native and AI-enabled companies, respectively. Notable recent funding rounds include $1.3 million in Seed funding for Aerotruth and $2 million for MagicBrief.','Goals 1 and 3 are partially answered, with information on sectors and funding landscape. Goals 2, 4, and 5 remain open, with no specific information on the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, geographic clusters, or growth rates of sectors.',1786417912807,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(54,'76fb1813',6,'https://www.startupdaily.net/','Australian AI startups are concentrated in sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with companies like Athena, Archistar, and Cluey Learning being examples. The funding landscape includes investors like AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia, with companies like Canva and Atlassian being notable examples of AI-native and AI-enabled companies, respectively. Recent funding rounds include $8.6 million for Vexev, $2.1 million for Enrola, and $2.85 billion for Firmus at a $15 billion valuation.','Goals 1, 2, and 3 are partially answered, with information on sectors, funding, and examples of AI-native and AI-enabled companies. Goals 4 and 5 are still open, with no specific information on geographic clusters or growth rates of sectors.',1786417982334,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(55,'76fb1813',7,'https://www.innovationaus.com/','South Australia has launched a royal commission into AI and has also partnered with OpenAI for potential research collaborations, data centre investment, and skills development. Additionally, the NRF has surpassed its $1.5 billion investment target, indicating a growing funding landscape for Australian AI startups.','Goals 1 and 5 are partially answered, with examples of AI startups in various sectors. Goals 2 and 3 are advanced, with information on the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies and the funding landscape. Goal 4 remains open, with no specific information on geographic clusters.',1786418049757,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(56,'76fb1813',8,'https://blackbird.vc/portfolio','Blackbird has invested in over 130 ambitious companies, including those in sectors such as healthcare, space technologies, and farming, leveraging artificial intelligence. Notable examples include Superstat, Tracksuit, and Hall, which have received investments from Blackbird. The funding landscape includes investors like Blackbird, with a focus on supporting founders and their life''s work.','Goals 2 and 3 have been partially advanced, with information on the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies and the funding landscape. However, goals 1, 4, and 5 remain open, with no specific information on growth rates, geographic clusters, or named example companies for each major sector.',1786418118940,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(57,'76fb1813',9,'https://techcouncil.com.au/','The Tech Council of Australia represents the nation''s leading technology companies, with 949,000 Australians employed in tech-related jobs and the industry contributing $248 billion to GDP. The council champions policies that drive tech sector growth, encourage investment, and support startups and scale-ups, including those in the AI sector. However, specific information on the growth rates of sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate, the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, and the differentiation of geographic clusters is not stated in the sources read so far.','Goals 1, 3, 4, and 5 are still open, while goal 2 has some progress with the understanding that AI-native companies are distinguished from AI-enabled incumbents, but the exact distinction is not clearly defined in the provided sources.',1786418191077,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(58,'76fb1813',10,'https://smallbizai.au/australian-ai-companies-complete-guide-by-industry-2026','Australian AI startups concentrate in sectors such as fintech, proptech, healthcare, and education, with examples including Athena, Archistar, and Cluey Learning. The funding landscape includes investors like AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia, with companies like Canva and Atlassian being notable examples of AI-native and AI-enabled companies, respectively. Two types of Australian AI companies are distinguished: those founded in 2016 or later, which built AI into their product from day one, and those founded before 2016, which added AI to existing products or workflows.','Goals 1, 2, and 3 are partially answered, while goals 4 and 5 are still open. The distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies is clarified, and the funding landscape is further detailed, but the growth rates of sectors and geographic clusters remain unclear.',1786418261377,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(59,'76fb1813',11,'https://startmate.com/portfolio','Startmate has invested in over 300 startups with a collective portfolio value of over $4.5 billion, including companies like Puralink, which provides autonomous robots for pipe inspection, and Landid, which harnesses AI to digitise property details. The portfolio includes companies in various sectors such as proptech, healthcare, and education, with examples including AI Voice Agents for real estate and AI-powered recruitment interviews.','Goals 1 and 3 are partially answered, with information on sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and the funding landscape. However, goals 2, 4, and 5 are still open, requiring more information on the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, geographic clusters, and named example companies for each major sector.',1786418329413,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(60,'76fb1813',12,'https://innovationaus.com/deep-tech-deal-surge-in-2026-as-nrf-gets-rolling','At least $1.8 billion was raised by Australian deep tech startups in the first quarter of 2026, with a trio of new tech unicorns emerging, and the federal government''s $15 billion industry fund investing in local sensor, space, robotics, and quantum companies.','Goals 1, 2, 4, and 5 are still open, while goal 3 has been partially advanced with information on the funding landscape, including the amount raised and the involvement of the federal government''s industry fund.',1786418398151,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(61,'98adcf63',1,'https://smallbizai.au/australian-ai-companies-complete-guide-by-industry-2026/','The Australian AI ecosystem includes companies like Canva, Atlassian, WiseTech, and REA Group, with a mix of AI-native startups and AI-enabled incumbents. Sectors mentioned include fintech, property technology, healthcare, and education. Notable investors include AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia. Companies like Airtasker, Athena, and Baraja are examples of AI-native startups, while Atlassian and REA Group are AI-enabled incumbents.','Goals 1, 2, 3, and 5 have been partially addressed, with some sectors and companies identified, as well as notable investors. Goals 4 remains open, with no information on geographic clusters.',1786418672103,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(62,'98adcf63',2,'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_and_technology_in_Australia','Not stated in the sources read so far regarding the main sectors where Australian and New Zealand AI startups concentrate, the distinction between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, the funding landscape, geographic clusters, or specific example companies for each major sector in 2026. However, prior findings and recalled sources mention companies like Canva, Atlassian, WiseTech, and REA Group, with sectors including fintech, property technology, healthcare, and education, and notable investors like AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia.','No new progress on any of the goals, as the provided source does not contain relevant information on the Australian and New Zealand AI startup ecosystem in 2026.',1786418744816,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(63,'98adcf63',3,'https://www.csiro.au/en/research/technology-space/ai','The Australian AI ecosystem includes companies like Canva, Atlassian, WiseTech, and REA Group, operating in sectors such as fintech, property technology, healthcare, and education, with notable investors including AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia. AI-native startups like Airtasker, Athena, and Baraja, and AI-enabled incumbents like Atlassian and REA Group are present. Geographic clusters include Sydney, Melbourne, and Perth, with companies like Airwallex and Brighte based in Melbourne and Sydney respectively.','Goals 2 and 5 are partially answered, with information on AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, as well as example companies for major sectors. Goals 1, 3, and 4 remain open, with no information on the main sectors where Australian and New Zealand AI startups concentrate, the funding landscape, or a comprehensive mapping of geographic clusters.',1786418817758,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(64,'98adcf63',4,'https://www.startmate.com/portfolio','Startmate''s portfolio includes over 300 startups with a collective value of over $4.5 billion, featuring companies like Puralink, Matilda, and Landid, operating in sectors such as robotics, migration, real estate, and healthcare, with some companies like Duohub and Medlo focusing on AI-related technologies','Goals 1, 3, and 4 remain open, while goals 2 and 5 have been partially addressed with the identification of AI-native companies and example companies for various sectors',1786418886110,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(65,'98adcf63',5,'https://www.cutthroughventure.com/reports','Australian startup funding rebounded to over $1 billion across Q3, with a $4 billion year, and Aussie startups raised $810m in Q2 as investor sentiment picked up. Notable investors include AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia, with companies like Canva, Atlassian, WiseTech, and REA Group operating in sectors such as fintech, property technology, healthcare, and education.','Goals 1 and 2 remain open, goal 3 has some progress with funding information, goals 4 and 5 are still unanswered',1786418959953,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(66,'98adcf63',6,'https://www.startupdaily.net/','Australian AI startups are concentrated in sectors such as fintech, property technology, healthcare, and education, with companies like Canva, Atlassian, WiseTech, and REA Group. Notable investors include AirTree Ventures, Blackbird, and Sequoia. AI-native startups like Airtasker, Athena, and Baraja, and AI-enabled incumbents like Atlassian and REA Group are present. Recent funding rounds include $8.6m for Vexev, $2.1m for Enrola, and $2.85 billion for Firmus at a $15B valuation.','Goals 1, 2, and 3 are partially answered, while goals 4 and 5 remain open. The main sectors and funding landscape are identified, but the distinction between AI-native and AI-enabled companies, geographic clusters, and specific example companies for each major sector require further research.',1786419031369,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(67,'98adcf63',7,'https://www.innovationaus.com/','South Australia is chasing OpenAI investment with a new MoU, and the NRF has surged past its $1.5bn investment target. Notable companies mentioned include Airwallex, Brighte, and Athena, operating in sectors such as fintech, property technology, and green finance. The Australian AI ecosystem includes a mix of AI-native startups and AI-enabled incumbents, with geographic clusters in Sydney, Melbourne, and Perth.','Goals 2, 3, and 5 have been partially advanced, with information on the distinction between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, the funding landscape, and example companies for each major sector. However, goals 1 and 4 remain open, with limited information on the main sectors where Australian and New Zealand AI startups concentrate and the geographic clusters.',1786419100988,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(68,'98adcf63',8,'https://blackbird.vc/portfolio','Blackbird has invested in over 130 ambitious companies, with a focus on AI-native startups and AI-enabled incumbents across various sectors, including healthcare, space technologies, and farming. Notable companies mentioned include Canva, Tracksuit, and Halter, with a presence in both Australia and New Zealand.','Goals 2 and 5 are partially answered, with a distinction between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, and example companies for each major sector. However, goals 1, 3, and 4 remain open, with further research needed to identify the main sectors, funding landscape, and geographic clusters.',1786419170046,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(69,'98adcf63',9,'https://techcouncil.com.au/','The Tech Council of Australia mentions the Australian technology industry contributing $248 billion to GDP, with 949,000 Australians employed in tech-related jobs, and notes the importance of driving growth, investment, and innovation in the tech sector. The council also highlights the need to support balanced, future-focused regulation that fosters innovation while ensuring security, privacy, and responsible AI development. Additionally, the council mentions the National Security Tech Alliance, Consumer Energy Tech Alliance, and the Australian Quantum Alliance as initiatives to drive innovation and growth in specific sectors.','Goals 2 and 3 have been partially advanced, with information on the distinction between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents and the funding landscape. However, more information is needed to fully answer these goals. Goals 1, 4, and 5 remain open.',1786419242213,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(70,'98adcf63',10,'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economy_of_New_Zealand','Not stated in the sources read so far regarding the main sectors where Australian and New Zealand AI startups concentrate, the distinction between AI-native companies and AI-enabled incumbents, the funding landscape, geographic clusters, or specific example companies for each major sector in 2026. However, New Zealand''s economy is diverse, with a strong primary sector, and the country has a highly efficient and strong economy, with a nominal GDP of US$248 billion. The economy is also heavily dependent on international trade, with a significant portion of its exports being agricultural products.','Goal 1 is partially addressed, but the main sectors where Australian and New Zealand AI startups concentrate are not specified. Goals 2-5 remain open.',1786419314298,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(71,'0f4fdd5c',1,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=New_Zealand&action=raw','The capital of New Zealand is Wellington, and the largest city is Auckland. Not stated in the sources read so far are the main sectors where New Zealand AI and technology startups concentrate, how AI-native companies are distinguished from AI-enabled incumbents, the funding landscape, or geographic clusters beyond the locations of the capital and largest city.','Only goal 4 (geographic clusters) has partial information, with Wellington as the capital and Auckland as the largest city. Goals 1, 2, and 3 are not addressed in the provided source.',1786420583327,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(72,'0f4fdd5c',2,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_New_Zealand&action=raw','New Zealand''s economy is divided into sectors, with 7% in agriculture, 19% in industry, and 65% in services (2018). The country has a high-income economy, with a GDP of $248.67 billion (nominal; 2025 forecast) and $298.93 billion (PPP; 2025). Not stated in the sources read so far are the specific sectors where New Zealand AI and technology startups concentrate, or how they are funded.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on New Zealand''s general economy sectors, but not specifically on AI and technology startups. Goals 2-5 remain open.',1786420658383,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(73,'0f4fdd5c',3,'https://www.callaghaninnovation.govt.nz/','The information technology sector in New Zealand is growing rapidly. Callaghan Innovation supports innovators and entrepreneurs in biotechnology, health technology, and other areas, and has worked with companies such as Biostart and Dot Ingredients to scale their products and technologies.','Goals 1 and 3 are partially answered, with information on the growth of the IT sector and the role of Callaghan Innovation in supporting startups. Goals 2, 4, and 5 remain open.',1786420727043,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(74,'0f4fdd5c',4,'https://creativehq.co.nz/','Creative HQ, based in Wellington, is a leading innovation hub that supports startups, founders, and innovators in New Zealand, with a focus on areas such as GovTech, Creative Tech, and climate innovation. The hub has supported over 400 startup founders since 2003 and provides services such as mentoring, coaching, and access to funding and networks.','Goals 1, 2, and 3 are still open, while goal 4 has been partially addressed with the identification of Wellington as a geographic cluster. Goal 5 is still open, but some information on specific companies and sectors has been provided.',1786420796421,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(75,'0f4fdd5c',5,'https://www.nzgcp.co.nz/','The New Zealand government has a $300m fund of funds, Elevate, which invests into venture capital funds to fill the Series A and B capital gap for high-growth New Zealand tech companies. The NZGCP also has an Aspire fund that invests directly into early-stage Kiwi technology start-ups at proof of concept, seed, and early expansion investment stages.','Goals 1, 2, 4, and 5 are still open. Goal 3 has been partially answered, with information on the funding landscape, including the Elevate and Aspire funds.',1786420866062,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(76,'d2cd8b42',1,'https://nzgcp.co.nz/','The New Zealand Growth Capital Partners'' Aspire fund invests directly into early-stage Kiwi technology start-ups at proof of concept, seed, and early expansion investment stages.','Goal 1 is partially answered, as one fund investing at seed stage in New Zealand has been identified, but it is unclear if there are other funds',1786493533235,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(77,'b8cc2adb',1,'https://nzgcp.co.nz/','The New Zealand Growth Capital Partners'' Aspire fund invests at the seed stage in New Zealand, targeting early-stage Kiwi technology start-ups','Goal 1 is partially answered, as one fund investing at seed stage in New Zealand has been identified, but it is unclear if there are other funds',1786497351329,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(78,'4306b012',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Not stated in the sources read so far','None of the goals are answered yet',1786550454035,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(79,'4306b012',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','The Tech Council of Australia supports the Prime Minister''s vision for developing and adopting AI in Australia, which is expected to attract investment, create jobs, and improve quality of life. The council also joined 11 other technology and innovation industry bodies in calling for changes to the proposed Innovative Business CGT Concession, which they believe falls short of supporting Australia''s startup technology sector.','Goals 1 and 2 are partially answered, with some information on the potential benefits of AI and the funding landscape, but more specific details on sectors, funding, and geographic clusters are still needed. Goal 3 remains open.',1786551547753,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(80,'4306b012',3,'https://innovationaus.com/feed','The technology sector in Australia is the fastest-growing productivity engine, contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP), with the startup sector responsible for creating high-growth, innovative businesses. However, the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate, their funding landscape, and geographic clusters are not stated in the sources read so far.','Goal 1 is partially addressed, but the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate are not stated. Goals 2 and 3 are not addressed.',1786552638759,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(81,'4306b012',4,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','The largest city in Australia is Sydney (metropolitan) and Melbourne (urban), according to the Australian Bureau of Statistics (ABS) Greater Capital City Statistical Areas (GCCSAs) and Significant Urban Areas (SUAs) respectively. However, the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate, their funding landscape, and what differentiates the geographic clusters are not stated in the sources read so far.','Goals 1 and 2 are still open, while goal 3 has some information about the largest cities but lacks details on the differentiation of geographic clusters',1786553736843,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(82,'4306b012',5,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','The technology sector in Australia is the fastest-growing productivity engine, contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP). The main sectors of the Australian economy are services (62.7%), construction (7.4%), mining (5.8%), manufacturing (5.8%), and agriculture (2.8%). However, the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate are not stated in the sources read so far.','Goal 1 is partially answered, Goal 2 and Goal 3 are still open',1786554831514,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(83,'9174a7bc',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Australian AI startups are present in the biotech sector, with 6 startups scoring $13.5 million from biotech grants fund CUREator+, indicating growth in the health tech and biotech areas','Goal 1 is partially answered, with biotech and health tech identified as sectors where Australian AI startups are present, but the fastest-growing sectors are not yet confirmed; Goal 2 remains open',1786596468377,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(84,'9174a7bc',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','The Australian tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering roles growing by 7% year-on-year and remaining the largest single technical occupational category. Technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the growth of technical roles, but Goal 2 remains open. The funding landscape and most active investors in Australian AI startups are still not identified.',1786597558847,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(85,'9174a7bc',3,'https://innovationaus.com/feed','The Australian technology sector contributes $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and is the fastest-growing productivity engine, with its growth underpinned by the startup sector. However, specific details on the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and their funding landscape are not stated in the sources read so far.','Goal 1 is partially answered with the identification of the biotech sector as a growing area, but the main sectors and fastest-growing sectors are not yet fully identified. Goal 2 remains open.',1786598647572,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(86,'9174a7bc',4,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','Not stated in the sources read so far are the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate, aside from biotech, and the funding landscape of Australian AI startups. However, the Australian technology sector contributes $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and is the fastest-growing productivity engine, with its growth underpinned by the startup sector. Australian AI startups are present in the biotech sector, with 6 startups scoring $13.5 million from biotech grants fund CUREator+.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with some information on the biotech sector, but the main sectors and growth rates of Australian AI startups are not fully identified. Goal 2 remains unanswered.',1786599742906,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(87,'9174a7bc',5,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','The Australian economy has a services sector that accounts for 62.7% of the economy, with other significant sectors including construction (7.4%), mining (5.8%), manufacturing (5.8%), and agriculture (2.8%). However, the sources do not specifically mention the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate, aside from biotech, which has seen 6 startups receive $13.5 million from the biotech grants fund CUREator+.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with some information on the broader Australian economy, but the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate, aside from biotech, and their growth rates are not stated in the sources read so far. Goal 2 remains unanswered.',1786600838785,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(88,'63ac5d92',1,NULL,'not stated in the sources read so far','none of the goals are answered, goal 1 is still open',1786605347040,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(89,'797a52f2',1,NULL,'not stated in the sources read so far','none of the goals are answered, all are still open',1786605403597,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(90,'ad74b95d',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Not stated in the sources read so far how spend is recorded per model','None of the goals are answered, goal 1 is still open',1786613411799,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(91,'5a8c9aeb',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Australian AI startups are found in sectors such as agtech (Farmbot) and biotech (6 startups scoring $13.5 million from CUREator+ grants), with funding rounds including $22 million Series B for Farmbot and $11.5 million Seed raise for Alloy Robotics, backed by the Big 3 VCs','Goals 1 and 2 are partially answered, with some sectors and funding information identified, but more information is needed to fully answer the goals',1786636839770,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(92,'5a8c9aeb',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','The Australian tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering roles growing by 7% year-on-year and remaining the largest single technical occupational category. Technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on sectors and growth rates, but Goal 2 remains open, with no new information on funding landscape or most active investors',1786637932552,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(93,'5a8c9aeb',3,NULL,'Australian AI startups cluster in sectors such as agtech and biotech, with notable funding rounds including $22 million Series B for Farmbot and $11.5 million Seed raise for Alloy Robotics. The tech sector contributes $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) to the Australian economy, with the startup sector driving growth and innovation.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with identified sectors including agtech and biotech. Goal 2 is partially answered, with notable funding rounds and investors mentioned, but more information on the funding landscape is needed.',1786639020997,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(94,'5a8c9aeb',4,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','The Australian tech sector contributes $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) to the economy and is the fastest-growing productivity engine, with the startup sector driving growth and innovation. However, the provided Wikipedia article does not mention specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate or details about their funding landscape.','Goal 1 is partially addressed with prior findings, but the Wikipedia article does not provide new information on the main sectors or funding landscape of Australian AI startups. Goal 2 remains unaddressed.',1786640112945,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(95,'5a8c9aeb',5,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','The Australian economy has a GDP of $1.950 trillion (nominal, 2026) and $2.060 trillion (PPP, 2025), with the tech sector contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and being the fastest-growing productivity engine. However, the provided Wikipedia article does not mention specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate or details about their funding landscape. Prior findings indicate Australian AI startups cluster in sectors such as agtech and biotech.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with prior findings indicating sectors such as agtech and biotech, but the provided Wikipedia article does not provide new information on this goal. Goal 2 remains unanswered.',1786641204171,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(96,'b099c83d',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Bailador, a listed VC, has survived the SAASpocalypse with PropHero as its FY26 lucky charm. A New Zealand AI startup, Stirling, has raised NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) in a round led by Blackbird. Kantoko, an ADHD startup founded by Zac Altman, has secured $3.5 million in seed funding.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has been partially answered with the identification of Blackbird as an active investor in Australian/NZ AI startups and the mention of specific funding rounds. Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) remains open.',1786723281116,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(97,'b099c83d',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','Australia''s tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering being the largest technical occupational category, growing by 7% year-on-year. Technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the tech workforce and technical occupational categories. Goal 2 remains open, with no new information on funding landscape or most active investors in Australian AI.',1786724375464,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(98,'b099c83d',3,NULL,'The Australian tech workforce has grown to approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with 424,000 in direct tech roles and 553,000 in technical roles embedded in other industries. Software engineering remains the largest technical occupational category, growing by 7% year-on-year.','Goal 1 has some information on the tech workforce and its growth, but the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and which are growing fastest are not yet fully identified. Goal 2 remains open, with no information yet on the most active investors in Australian AI, typical stages, and notable recent rounds.',1786725467274,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(99,'b099c83d',4,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','Australia''s technology sector is its fastest-growing productivity engine, contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and employing nearly a million people. The sector''s growth is underpinned by the startup sector, which creates high-growth, innovative businesses that create jobs and boost exports and innovation across every industry.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the tech sector''s contribution to GDP and employment. Goal 2 is still open, with no new information on funding landscape, active investors, or notable recent rounds.',1786726563255,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(100,'b099c83d',5,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','Australia''s technology sector, which includes AI startups, is its fastest-growing productivity engine, contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and employing nearly a million people. The sector''s growth is underpinned by the startup sector, with software engineering being the largest technical occupational category, growing by 7% year-on-year.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the technology sector''s contribution to GDP and employment. However, the specific sectors where Australian AI startups cluster and which are growing fastest are not yet fully identified. Goal 2 remains open, with no information yet on the most active investors in Australian AI, typical stages, and notable recent rounds.',1786727655092,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(101,'dc0a0b39',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Bailador, a listed VC, has survived the SAASpocalypse with PropHero as its FY26 lucky charm. A New Zealand AI startup, Stirling, has raised NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) in a round led by Blackbird. Kantoko, an ADHD startup founded by Zac Altman, has landed $3.5M in seed funding.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has some information, but Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) is not addressed in the provided material. The funding landscape is partially mapped with Blackbird as an active investor and notable recent rounds including Stirling''s $3.15 million and Kantoko''s $3.5 million.',1786809642743,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(102,'dc0a0b39',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','The Australian tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering being the largest technical occupational category, growing by 7% year-on-year. Technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall. Notable funding rounds include Stirling''s NZ$3.8 million, Kantoko''s $3.5M, and Alloy Robotics'' $11.5 million.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the tech workforce and job growth, but Goal 2 remains open, with only limited information on funding landscape and investors.',1786810739767,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(103,'dc0a0b39',3,NULL,'Notable funding rounds in the Australian AI startup ecosystem include Stirling''s NZ$3.8 million, Kantoko''s $3.5M, and Alloy Robotics'' $11.5 million. The Australian tech workforce has grown, with software engineering being the largest technical occupational category, and technical jobs in regional Australia growing by 12% over 5 years.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has some information, but more details on most active investors and typical stages are still needed. Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) remains largely unanswered.',1786811828978,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(104,'dc0a0b39',4,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','The Australian tech workforce has grown to approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering being the largest technical occupational category, growing by 7% year-on-year. Technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall. Notable funding rounds include Stirling''s NZ$3.8 million, Kantoko''s $3.5M, and Alloy Robotics'' $11.5 million. However, the provided Wikipedia article does not mention the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate or the most active investors in Australian AI.','Goal 1 is still open, as the provided sources do not specify the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate. Goal 2 has some progress, with notable funding rounds mentioned, but the most active investors and typical stages are not fully identified.',1786812921764,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(105,'dc0a0b39',5,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','The Australian economy has a services sector that accounts for 62.7% of the economy, with other sectors including construction (7.4%), mining (5.8%), manufacturing (5.8%), and agriculture (2.8%) as of 2017. However, the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate are not stated in the sources read so far.','Goal 1 is partially answered with information on the general economy sectors, but the specific sectors for Australian AI startups are still unknown. Goal 2 remains unanswered.',1786814017049,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(106,'8772de4e',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Bailador, a listed VC, has survived the SAASpocalypse with PropHero as its FY26 lucky charm. A New Zealand AI startup, Stirling, has raised NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) in a round led by Blackbird. Kantoko, an ADHD startup founded by Zac Altman, has landed $3.5M in seed funding.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has been partially answered with the identification of Blackbird as an active investor in Australian/NZ AI startups and the mention of specific funding rounds. Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) remains open.',1786896053025,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(107,'8772de4e',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','Australia''s tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering remaining the largest technical occupational category, growing by 7% year-on-year. Technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall. Notable funding rounds include Stirling''s NZ$3.8 million raise led by Blackbird, Kantoko''s $3.5M seed funding, and Alloy Robotics'' $11.5m seed raise backed by Australia''s VC trinity.','Goal 1 is partially answered with the identification of software engineering as a major sector, and goal 2 is partially answered with the mention of specific funding rounds and investors such as Blackbird and Australia''s VC trinity.',1786897148352,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(108,'8772de4e',3,NULL,'The Australian tech sector is currently contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and is the fastest-growing productivity engine, with the startup sector underpinning its growth. Notable funding rounds include Stirling''s NZ$3.8 million raise, Kantoko''s $3.5M seed funding, and Alloy Robotics'' $11.5m seed raise.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the tech sector''s growth, but the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate are not yet identified. Goal 2 is also partially answered, with some information on funding rounds, but the most active investors and typical stages are not yet fully mapped.',1786898239968,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(109,'8772de4e',4,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','Not stated in the sources read so far which sectors Australian AI startups concentrate in, or how they are funded, as the provided Wikipedia article does not contain relevant information on the Australian AI startup ecosystem.','Neither of the goals is answered yet.',1786899330230,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(110,'8772de4e',5,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','The Australian tech sector is currently contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and is the fastest-growing productivity engine. However, the provided sources still do not specify which sectors Australian AI startups concentrate in. Notable funding rounds include Stirling''s NZ$3.8 million raise, Kantoko''s $3.5M seed funding, and Alloy Robotics'' $11.5m seed raise.','Goal 1 remains unfulfilled as the sources do not specify the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate. Goal 2 has some information on funding rounds but lacks a comprehensive mapping of the funding landscape.',1786900422568,NULL);
