INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(121,'ee963b00',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Bailador, a listed VC, has survived the SAASpocalypse with PropHero as its FY26 lucky charm. Additionally, a New Zealand AI startup, Stirling, has raised NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) in a round led by Blackbird. Other funding news includes Kantoko raising $3.5 million for its ADHD startup, Farmbot raising $22 million in a Series B for its US push, and 6 startups scoring $13.5 million from biotech grants fund CUREator+. Alloy Robotics has also raised $11.5 million in a seed round backed by the Big 3 VCs.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has been partially answered with information on recent funding rounds and investors, but Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) remains open.',1786933347352,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(122,'7d48524f',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Australian AI startups are funded by investors such as Blackbird, with a recent example being Stirling, a New Zealand AI startup, raising NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) in a round led by Blackbird. Other sectors mentioned include agtech, with Farmbot raising $22 million Series B, and biotech, with six Aussie biotechs receiving $13.5m in CUREator+ grants.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has been partially answered, with some active investors and recent funding rounds identified. Goal 1 (main sectors and growth) is still open, although some sectors have been mentioned.',1786933355556,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(123,'4409e2de',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Bailador, a listed VC, has survived the SAASpocalypse with PropHero as its FY26 lucky charm. Additionally, several startups have received funding, including Stirling, which raised NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) led by Blackbird, and Alloy Robotics, which landed $11.5m from Australia’s VC trinity. Other funded startups include Kantoko, which received $3.5 million, and Farmbot, which raised $22 million Series B. Six Aussie biotechs also grabbed $13.5m in CUREator+ grants.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has been partially answered with the identification of active investors such as Blackbird and the VC trinity, as well as notable recent funding rounds. Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) remains open.',1786933369789,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(124,'9ba1fba2',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','A New Zealand AI startup, Stirling, has raised NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) in funding, led by Blackbird. Another startup, Kantoko, founded by Zac Altman, has raised $3.5 million in seed funding. Farmbot, an agtech startup, has secured $22 million in Series B funding. Six Australian biotechs have received $13.5 million in grants from CUREator+ to develop AI health, cancer, and heart tech.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has been partially answered with information on specific funding rounds, but Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) remains open.',1786934728134,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(125,'a1a7886d',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','A New Zealand AI startup, Stirling, has raised NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) in funding, led by Blackbird. Another startup, Kantoko, has raised $3.5 million in seed funding for its ADHD-focused health tech. Farmbot, an agtech company, has secured $22 million in Series B funding. Six Australian biotechs have received $13.5 million in grants from CUREator+ for AI health, cancer, and heart tech projects.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has been partially answered with information on specific funding rounds, but Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) remains unanswered.',1786934736581,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(126,'aa500e30',1,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','Not stated in the sources read so far regarding the sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate or their funding landscape','Neither of the two goals is answered',1786934860820,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(127,'65d8cb5a',1,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','Not stated in the sources read so far which sectors Australian AI startups concentrate in or how they are funded. The provided source is about general information on Australia, including its geography, government, economy, and demographics, but does not mention AI startups.','Neither of the goals is answered yet',1786934870811,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(128,'016c53e6',1,'https://techboard.com.au/feed','Techboard has published reports on unannounced investments in Australian startups and tech companies, as well as artificial intelligence funding data reviews from FY18 to FY25, but the provided material does not specify the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate or the most active investors in Australian AI.','Goal 1 is still open, Goal 2 has some relevant information but not enough to fully answer it',1786935246499,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(129,'0341c91a',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Australian AI startup Sophiie AI has landed a $5 million Seed round, and another AI startup, Stirling, from New Zealand, has raised NZ$3.8 million (A$3.15m) in funding. The sectors mentioned include AI, fintech, agtech, and biotech. Notable investors mentioned include Blackbird.','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has been partially answered with information on specific funding rounds and investors, but more information is needed on the most active investors and typical stages. Goal 1 (main sectors and growth) has been partially answered with mentions of various sectors, but more information is needed on which sectors are growing the fastest.',1786939701120,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(130,'ec5d3909',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Australian AI startups are found in sectors such as travel (Visaible.ai), finance (Stirling), and business strategy (Canva, Sophiie AI), with funding rounds including $1 million for Visaible.ai, $5 million for Sophiie AI, and $3.15 million for Stirling, led by investors like Blackbird','Some sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate have been identified, as well as some funding information, but the fastest growing sectors and a comprehensive funding landscape are still unknown',1786982496159,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(131,'ec5d3909',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','The Australian AI startup ecosystem has companies in sectors such as fintech, biotechnology, medical technology, digital health, space, robotics, agritech, climate, education, and sports technology. The Tech Council of Australia represents over 170 companies in these sectors. Recent funding rounds include $5 million for Sophiie AI and $3.15 million for Stirling, a New Zealand AI startup. The Australian tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with more than half holding technical roles outside direct tech firms.','Goal 1 is partially answered with the identification of sectors, and Goal 2 is partially answered with the mention of funding rounds and investors. However, more information is needed to fully answer both goals.',1786983590888,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(132,'ec5d3909',3,NULL,'Australian AI startups cluster in sectors such as fintech, biotechnology, medical technology, digital health, space, robotics, agritech, climate, education, and sports technology, with recent funding rounds including $5 million for Sophiie AI and $3.15 million for Stirling. The Tech Council of Australia represents over 170 companies in these sectors. Notably, technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall, indicating a growing demand for technical skills across the economy.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with identified sectors and some funding information, but growth rates of specific sectors are not stated in the sources read so far. Goal 2 is partially answered, with some funding rounds and investors mentioned, but a comprehensive mapping of the funding landscape is still missing.',1786984681272,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(133,'ec5d3909',4,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','Not stated in the sources read so far regarding the specific sectors where Australian AI startups are growing fastest or the most active investors in Australian AI. However, the sources recall that Australian AI startups cluster in sectors such as fintech, biotechnology, medical technology, digital health, space, robotics, agritech, climate, education, and sports technology, with recent funding rounds including $5 million for Sophiie AI and $3.15 million for Stirling.','Goal 1 is partially answered, goal 2 remains open',1786985773843,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(134,'ec5d3909',5,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','The main sectors of the Australian economy are services (62.7%), construction (7.4%), mining (5.8%), manufacturing (5.8%), and agriculture (2.8%), but the sources do not specify which sectors Australian AI startups concentrate in or which are growing fastest. However, recalled sources suggest Australian AI startups cluster in sectors such as fintech, biotechnology, medical technology, digital health, space, robotics, agritech, climate, education, and sports technology.','Goal 1 is partially answered, Goal 2 remains open',1786986867414,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(135,'f9da95d4',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Australian AI startups are found in sectors such as travel (Visaible.ai), construction (Sophiie AI), and data centers (NextDC), with funding rounds including $1 million for Visaible.ai and $5 million for Sophiie AI','Some sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate have been identified, and some funding information is available, but more information is needed to fully answer the goals',1787068851245,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(136,'f9da95d4',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','The Australian tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering roles growing by 7% year-on-year, and technical jobs in regional Australia growing by 12% over 5 years. The Tech Council of Australia supports the Prime Minister''s vision to develop and adopt AI in Australia, which is expected to attract investment, create new jobs, and lift productivity.','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the growth of technical roles, but Goal 2 remains open, with no new information on funding landscape or notable recent rounds',1787069945453,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(137,'f9da95d4',3,NULL,'The Australian technology sector contributes $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and is underpinned by the startup sector, which creates high-growth, innovative businesses, but the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and their funding landscape remain to be fully identified','Goal 1 is partially answered, Goal 2 is still open',1787071033084,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(138,'f9da95d4',4,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','Not stated in the sources read so far regarding the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and their funding landscape, but the Australian technology sector contributes $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and the startup sector creates high-growth, innovative businesses','Goal 1 is still open, Goal 2 is still open',1787072126711,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(139,'f9da95d4',5,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','The Australian economy has a highly developed mixed economy with various sectors, including services (62.7%), construction (7.4%), mining (5.8%), manufacturing (5.8%), and agriculture (2.8%). However, the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and their funding landscape remain to be fully identified. The Australian technology sector contributes $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) and is underpinned by the startup sector, which creates high-growth, innovative businesses.','Goal 1 is partially answered, but the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and their funding landscape remain to be fully identified. Goal 2 is not yet answered.',1787073218601,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(140,'9c936389',1,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','The Australian tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering roles growing by 7% year-on-year and remaining the largest single technical occupational category (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed). Technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed).','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the tech workforce and technical occupational categories, but more information is needed on the specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and which are growing fastest. Goal 2 is not yet addressed.',1787085234326,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(141,'9c936389',2,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','The Australian technology sector is the country''s fastest-growing productivity engine, contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed), with the startup sector driving this growth by creating high-growth, innovative businesses (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed).','Goal 2 (funding landscape) has some information, but details on most active investors, typical stages, and notable recent rounds are still missing. Goal 1 (main sectors of Australian AI startups) remains largely unanswered.',1787085259734,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(142,'9c936389',3,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Economy_of_Australia&action=raw','The Australian technology sector is a significant contributor to the country''s economy, with a contribution of $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed), and the startup sector is driving this growth by creating high-growth, innovative businesses (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed). Additionally, the sector is the country''s fastest-growing productivity engine (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed). However, the main sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate and the funding landscape, including most active investors, typical stages, and notable recent rounds, are not stated in the sources read so far.','Goal 1 is not yet answered, and Goal 2 is partially answered, but the funding landscape is still unclear.',1787085290421,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(143,'f2539796',1,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','The Australian tech workforce reached approximately 977,000 people by November 2025, with software engineering roles growing by 7% year-on-year and remaining the largest single technical occupational category (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed). Technical jobs in regional Australia grew by 12% over 5 years, more than twice the growth rate for regional jobs overall (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed).','Goal 1 is partially answered, with information on the size and growth of the tech workforce, but Goal 2 remains open',1787086955566,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(144,'f2539796',2,'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Australia&action=raw','Australia''s technology sector is its fastest-growing productivity engine, contributing $248.5 billion (8.9% of GDP) (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed), and the startup sector is responsible for creating high-growth, innovative businesses that create jobs, boost exports and innovation across every industry (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed).','Goal 1 is partially answered, as we know the tech sector is a significant contributor to the economy, but we still need to identify specific sectors where Australian AI startups concentrate. Goal 2 is also partially answered, as we have information on the tech sector''s growth and contribution to GDP, but we still need to map the funding landscape and identify most active investors in Australian AI.',1787088046659,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(145,'ed43c125',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Visaible.ai raised $1 million (https://startupdaily.net/feed), Sophiie AI raised $5 million in a Seed round (https://startupdaily.net/feed), and Space Angel received a $1.75 million grant (https://startupdaily.net/feed), while Orivium is seeking $30 million in a Series B (https://startupdaily.net/feed), and Canva''s valuation was reduced by $11 billion (https://startupdaily.net/feed).','Goal 1 is partially answered, with several new funding events recorded. Goal 2 is not yet addressed as there is no baseline to compare with.',1787088152021,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(146,'0540d791',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Visaible.ai received $1 million in funding (https://startupdaily.net/feed), Sophiie AI landed a $5 million Seed round (https://startupdaily.net/feed), and Space Angel was granted $1.75 million by the WA government (https://startupdaily.net/feed).','Goal 1 is partially answered, Goal 2 is not yet addressed as there is no baseline to compare with.',1787088215762,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(147,'35e0c08b',1,'https://startupdaily.net/feed','Nybro, a biotech company, has doubled its Seed round to $20 million, supported by QIC Ventures (https://startupdaily.net/feed).','Goal 1 is partially answered, with one new funding event recorded. Goal 2 is not applicable yet as there is no baseline to compare with.',1787155322248,NULL);
INSERT INTO "findings" ("id","run_id","n","source_url","finding","progress","created_at","leaked") VALUES(148,'35e0c08b',2,'https://techcouncil.com.au/feed','No new Australian AI or tech funding events were found in the provided source (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed), but recalled sources (https://startupdaily.net/feed) mention that Sophiie AI landed a $5 million Seed round (https://startupdaily.net/feed) and Visaible.ai found room for $1 million (https://startupdaily.net/feed), which are already recorded. The source (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed) discusses the Australian tech workforce and the Tech Council''s response to the Prime Minister''s AI speech, but does not mention any new funding events (https://techcouncil.com.au/feed).','Goal 1 is partially advanced, as no new funding events were found, but prior findings and recalled sources were considered.',1787156422351,'["Sophiie AI","Visaible.ai"]');
