INSERT INTO "control" ("key","value") VALUES('daily_brief','{"topic":"Australian and New Zealand AI and tech funding: track new events daily and flag divergence from the baseline.","goals":["Record every new AI or tech funding event in today''s sources: company, sector, amount, stage, investors, date, COUNTRY. Report only events not already in the ledger. State the country only where the material says or clearly implies it — a ''Kiwi'' startup or one based in Auckland is New Zealand; Sydney, Melbourne, Brisbane, Perth and Canberra are Australia. Where it does not, write ''-''. Do not infer a country from the publication.","Flag where today''s events diverge from the baseline''s SECTOR taxonomy: a funded company whose sector maps onto NONE of the taxonomy''s rows. A sector that maps onto a row under a different name is not a divergence — the test is ''does not map'', not ''is not listed verbatim''. ONLY for companies in the country the baseline covers: it is an Australian baseline, so a New Zealand or other company diverges from nothing and must not be flagged. Do NOT judge round size: code checks that against the baseline''s own flag table. Do NOT flag investors: the baseline ranks none, so an unfamiliar investor is evidence of nothing."],"sources":["https://www.startupdaily.net/feed/"],"maxIterations":1}');
INSERT INTO "control" ("key","value") VALUES('baseline',replace('# AU tech & AI funding baseline — H1 2026\n\nSet 2026-08-20. Comparison period: Q1 2026 vs Q2 2026 (same taxonomy).\nPrior year for scale only: calendar 2025.\n\n**Country coverage: AU.** Every figure here is Australian (Cut Through). A round\nraised anywhere else cannot be checked against B1, B3 or B4 — there is no\nbaseline for it, and that is not the same as it being unremarkable. The code\nreads this line; it is the declaration, not a description of one.\n\n## B1 · Sector distribution — H1 2026\n\nShare is of the **$3.5B raised across H1 2026**, not of the listed rows. Share is\nthe unit to compare against, not the dollar amount: quarters differ in size, so a\nsector can grow its dollars and lose its share.\n\n| sector | H1 2026 | share | Q1 | Q2 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| AI models & data infrastructure | $830M | 23.7% | $100M | $730M |\n| Vertical business software | $518M | 14.8% | $447M | $71M |\n| Fintech | $483M+ | 13.8%+ | not in top 10 | $483M |\n| Hardware, robotics & sensors | $420M | 12.0% | $303M | $117M |\n| Space & defence | $293M | 8.4% | $229M | $64M |\n| Healthtech | $187M | 5.3% | $76M | $111M |\n| Cybersecurity, compliance & digital identity | $143M | 4.1% | $125M | $18M |\n| Climate & energy | $132M | 3.8% | $79M | $53M |\n| Crypto, Web3 & stablecoins | $113M | 3.2% | $113M | not listed |\n| Horizontal business software | $104M | 3.0% | $78M | $26M |\n| Consumer brands | $80M | 2.3% | $80M | not listed |\n| Life sciences & biotech | $31M+ | 0.9%+ | not in top 10 | $31M |\n| Marketplace | $9M+ | 0.3%+ | not in top 10 | $9M |\n| *unlisted* | *$157M* | *4.5%* | | |\n\nVolume: Q1 2026 $1.8B / 81 venture + 26 accelerator rounds; Q2 2026 $1.7B /\n64 venture + 5 accelerator.\n\nDeal counts published: Q1 vertical business software 30, hardware/robotics 17.\nQ2 vertical business software 15, climate & energy 11, hardware/robotics 8,\nlife sciences & biotech 8, fintech 6, healthtech 6. No other sector has one.\n\n**Fastest growing Q1→Q2 2026:** AI models & data infrastructure +630%\n($100M→$730M, 5.6%→42.6% of the quarter); healthtech +46%. Fintech rose from\noutside the top ten to second. **Sharpest falls:** cybersecurity −86%, vertical\nbusiness software −84%, space & defence −72%, horizontal business software −67%.\n\n**Quarterly volume, published figures:**\n\n| quarter | announced | rounds |\n|---|---|---|\n| Q1 2025 | $993M | 100 |\n| Q2 2025 | $812M | 76 |\n| Q3 2025 | ~$1.0B | 116 (85 venture + 31 accelerator) |\n| Q4 2025 | **~$2.6B — DERIVED**, see below | ~98 |\n| Q1 2026 | $1.8B | 107 |\n| Q2 2026 | $1.7B | 69 |\n\nQ4 2025 is **not published**; it is CY2025 minus the three quarters above. Three\ndifferent CY2025 totals circulate — $5.4B (Cut Through), $5.48B and $5.1B — so\nthat subtraction carries roughly ±$400M on a ~$2.6B figure. Use it for shape,\nnever as a number.\n\nPrior year: CY2025 $5.4B across 390 deals, +31% YoY, third-largest on record —\nAI $1.0B, fintech $868M, biotech/medtech $829M (49 deals, the deal-count\nleader). 61% of all capital went to startups building with AI in the stack.\n\n## B3 · Median round size by stage\n\n| stage | CY2025 | Q1 2026 | Q2 2026 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Angel + Pre-Seed | $1.0M | $1.2M | $1.3M |\n| Seed | $2.5M | $6.1M | $4.0M |\n| Series A | $11.0M | $12.5M | $18.6M |\n| Series B+ | $30.0M | $27M | $41M |\n\nSeries A has nearly doubled in eighteen months; seed spiked in Q1 and fell back.\n\n**Divergence rule — CONSTRUCTED, NOT MEASURED.** Cut Through publishes medians,\nnot ranges, so these bounds are a stated choice (⅓× to 3× the Q2 2026 median),\nnot an observed distribution. Flag a round outside:\n\n| stage | flag below | flag above |\n|---|---|---|\n| Angel / Pre-Seed | $0.4M | $3.9M |\n| Seed | $1.3M | $12.0M |\n| Series A | $6.2M | $55.8M |\n| Series B+ | $13.7M | $123M |\n\nA round with no stage stated cannot be checked against this table. Say the\nstage was absent rather than assuming one.\n\n## B2 · Most active investors — NOT MEASURED\n\nNo source ranks Australian investors by deal count. Cut Through publishes no\ninvestor leaderboard across its whole insights catalogue; the ranked lists that\nsurface in search are SEO aggregator pages whose counts cite nothing.\n\n**Do not flag investor divergence.** An unfamiliar investor is not evidence of\nanything while this section is empty. This is a gap in the baseline, not a\nfinding about the market.\n\n## B4 · Watchlist\n\n**Sectors** (the B1 taxonomy). Two things are reportable: a funded company whose\nsector does not map onto any row below, and a run of rounds in a sector whose\nH1 share was under 5% (healthtech, cybersecurity, climate & energy, crypto,\nhorizontal business software, consumer brands, life sciences, marketplace).\nThe taxonomy:\nAI models & data infrastructure · vertical business software · fintech ·\nhardware, robotics & sensors · space & defence · healthtech · cybersecurity,\ncompliance & digital identity · climate & energy · crypto, Web3 & stablecoins ·\nhorizontal business software · consumer brands · life sciences & biotech ·\nmarketplace.\n\n**Investors seen in AU venture** — membership only, NOT a ranking (see B2):\nBlackbird, AirTree, Square Peg, Main Sequence, Artesian, OIF, Rampersand,\nFolklore, Tenacious, King River, Skip Capital, Telstra Ventures.\n\n## Coverage limits — read these before flagging\n\n1. **Q1''s sector list is a top ten.** It sums to $1.63B of a stated $1.8B, so\n   ~$170M sits in sectors it does not name. "Not in top 10" means *below $76M*,\n   not zero. Q2''s eleven entries sum to $1.71B against a stated $1.7B, so that\n   quarter is effectively complete.\n2. **The 2025 taxonomy is different** — "Artificial Intelligence",\n   "Biotech/Medtech" — so only fintech survives the boundary unchanged. Do not\n   compute growth across it.\n3. **One quarter is one observation.** AI''s +630% is a single quarter-on-quarter\n   move on a base of $100M, and Q2''s $730M is concentrated enough that one large\n   round could dominate it. Treat it as the direction, not the rate.\n4. Grants and government money (QIC Ventures, state programmes) are not venture\n   rounds and are not in these figures.\n\n## Provenance\n\n- Cut Through Quarterly 2Q 2026 — https://www.cutthrough.com/insights/cut-through-quarterly-2q-2026\n- Cut Through Quarterly 1Q 2026 — https://www.cutthrough.com/insights/cut-through-quarterly-1q-2026\n- State of Australian Startup Funding 2025 — https://www.cutthrough.com/insights/state-of-australian-startup-funding-2025\n- Cut Through Quarterly 3Q 2025 / 2Q 2025 / 1Q 2025 — same path, `cut-through-quarterly-<q>q-2025`.\n  Q3 2025 publishes **no sector dollars and no stage medians**, which is why the\n  sector table stops at H1 2026 rather than running a trailing twelve months.\n- Investor-ranking absence confirmed against https://www.cutthrough.com/insights (full catalogue)\n','\n',char(10)));
